% ============================================================================
% circuit-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics circuit-parts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does the switch do in
% a circuit?": it states no physics fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `circuit_part_role` rows and returns the role + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fifth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the role
% `carries_current`, recall the part that does it — the wire). A capacitor is
% not one of these basic parts, so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a role.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli circuit-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "circuit-parts.adj"

? circuit_part_role(battery, $Role)          % expect provides_dc_power
? circuit_part_role(switch, $Role)           % expect opens_or_closes
? circuit_part_role(lamp, $Role)             % expect converts_to_light
? circuit_part_role(resistor, $Role)         % expect slows_current
? circuit_part_role($Part, carries_current)  % expect wire — reverse recall
? circuit_part_role(capacitor, $Role)        % expect abstain — not a basic part here
